<item>
  <title>New paper: BathyBoard, a surfboard-based platform for surf zone bathymetry (ASCE Journal of Surveying Engineering)</title>
  <link>https://tsampras.ucsd.edu/news/2026-11-new-paper-bathyboard/</link>
  <description><![CDATA[ 




<p>The BathyBoard paper is now published in the ASCE <em>Journal of Surveying Engineering</em>. The BathyBoard is a low-cost survey platform that carries an echo sounder and a GNSS receiver on a surfboard. It can be flown to remote sites, works safely around swimmers and surfers, and measures bathymetry close to breaking waves in water too shallow for survey jet skis. The work is part of the Functional Surfing Reef project.</p>
<p>Kanoa Pick, Kaden Quinn, Nicholas Cirrito, Ashton Domi, Georgios Tsampras, Falk Feddersen (2026), BathyBoard: A Surfboard-Based Platform for Measuring Surf Zone Bathymetry, <em>Journal of Surveying Engineering</em>, 153(1), 04026014, DOI: <a href="https://doi.org/10.1061/JSUED2.SUENG-1758">10.1061/JSUED2.SUENG-1758</a></p>



<a onclick="window.scrollTo(0, 0); return false;" id="quarto-back-to-top"><i class="bi bi-arrow-up"></i> Back to top</a> ]]></description>
